<!--Post: 2716--><!--Time: 1104010972-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2716"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Victoria<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Victoria<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 25, 2004 - 1:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Where would a killer keep mementos for decades without fear that any thing, except death, could expose them? Any ideas? I suggest looking at SDB kept by males for decades.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2716-->
<!--Post: 2719--><!--Time: 1104023247-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2719"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 25, 2004 - 5:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good thought Victoria, but, if i&#39;m not mistaken, a warrant is needed for that.  Safety deposit boxes are EXTREMELY priviledged.  Sufficient evidence would be needed for ONE bank; let alone ALL banks.  So, let&#39;s find some evidence.  I like that theory.  So obvious, yet I don&#39;t believe ever spoken about.  Good work!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2719-->
<!--Post: 2734--><!--Time: 1104037250-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2734"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 25, 2004 - 9:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I predict BTK has the items at his residence and that they are unbelievably well-hidden. But I love <BR>the safety deposit box idea. It&#39;s very solid. The thing is, BTK trusts <b>nobody</b> and that may include any bank. BTK also probably uses the mementos as fantasy fodder and that points toward keeping things at home. But Victoria you&#39;ve given me a great idea, thank you!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2734-->
<!--Post: 2735--><!--Time: 1104037536-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2735"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dawgar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dawgar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 25, 2004 - 9:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->good idea victoria <BR>but i think george is correct about the mementos and that he probably doesnt trust anything or person.. <BR>having said that...this guy isnt typical so the bank idea is possible<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2735-->
<!--Post: 2757--><!--Time: 1104080333-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2757"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Victoria<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Victoria<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 26, 2004 - 8:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My first post, so thanks for the encouragment. SDV contents are privileged, but do you think the police could get a list of people who have kept SDB for decades?  <BR> <BR>I just can&#39;t imagine where he would keep the evidence. In his house? Buried in the back yard?Wouldn&#39;t that mean he could never leave home? 25 years is a long time without a vacation or illness. Too risky. Any ideas on hiding places?  <BR> <BR>As far as SDB you have your own little room and can stay as long as you like. Sure, police need a warrant to go inside a box, but would they need one to take a look at a list of owners?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2757-->
<!--Post: 2802--><!--Time: 1104158823-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2802"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 6:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Letters Testamentary will get one in as well. Of course that will only help if BTK is dead. He could have a room in a storage facility as well. They are very respectful of privacy at those places. All he has to do is make his payments; and if he is wise he will have paid years in advance. If BTK is a do-it-yourselfer, one would have to dismantle his residence to find things that he has hidden. One can also hid things within a vehicle, boat, RV, hangar, airplane &#40;except at annual time&#41;, etc.  Whatever and wherever he has his mementos, you can be assured that he has prepared for every scenario including his demise, whether natural, accidental, etc. If he is a  traveler, he may have his stash in any number of places. Only he can put all the puzzle pieces together. Dean Coryll used a stoarge facility to hide bodies. No one even complained about any odor. <BR> <BR>Of course, there was the man who stored his deceased wife&#39;s body at his brother&#39;s home for quite awhile. Eventually they got tired of it and curious and opened it and found the mummified remains. I do not think that BTK is that stupid, however.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2802-->
<!--Post: 3047--><!--Time: 1104380944-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3047"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 8:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Victoria...  I do not believe a warrant is needed to see a list of names of SDB renters, but, keep in mind, that the police would find a lot of renters that have had them for 25&#43; years.  I have found that the elderly DO NOT like change and will keep their SDB until death.  Also, as far as the privacy issue, TWO keys are needed to open the box; the master that the bank manager keeps and the key the customer keeps.  If the customer&#39;s key is lost, the bank charges a huge fee to cut open the box as that is the only other way to open it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3047-->
<!--Post: 3050--><!--Time: 1104382711-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3050"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 8:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Im only curious Dee, but what happens if a person dies and payment obviously ceases.  Is there a statute of limitations allowing the bank access to its contents? I would think B would want all his momentos close at hand to look at from time to time.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3050-->
<!--Post: 3067--><!--Time: 1104417827-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3067"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 6:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->squirrel...  In the event of death, the SDB becomes the ward of the &#34;state&#34;.  I put state in quotes because if there is no will, the contents get rolled up in the whole probate mess.  If there is a will, the contents automatically become property of the heir; unless otherwise specified in the will.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3067-->
<!--Post: 3435--><!--Time: 1104893331-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3435"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 6:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks for the info Dee.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3435-->
<!--Post: 4531--><!--Time: 1106494942-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4531"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Victoria<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Victoria<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 7:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The only way to catch BTK is going to be through boring, slow clerical work. People working in banks should be contacted and send names in for SDB&#39;s owned for over 25 years by males. There is usually a nice little private room renters can use. You can stay as long as you want. Mine costs $40 a year. It is belongs only to me. This is where I would look. Or, as I expect, the police have a pretty good idea who BTK is. They just need evidence &amp; have to catch him in the act. Remember, the Unibomber wasn&#39;t online. His brother gave him up. Ted Bundy WENT to Florida where he KNEW they had the death penalty. He wanted to get caught. BTK does not. See my query regarding getting crossword puzzle experts involved. I have already asked remote viewers of IRVA.org, to have their students on the case. They should post on catchbtk.com. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4531-->
<!--Post: 4533--><!--Time: 1106498990-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4533"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 8:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Victoria - I agree that it will probably take clerical research and the SDB is an excellent idea...get the list of names of all the SDB holders within 50-75 miles &amp; compare to the other databases...see if anyone pops out/matches up...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4533-->
<!--Post: 5815--><!--Time: 1107390644-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5815"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brown_tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brown_tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 4:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t believe BTK has items stashed at his home. Why? Why would he? If he did, he&#39;d be inclined to look at them, smell them and keep reliving whatever made him do the crimes in the first place. But because &#40;as far as we know&#41; no murders have been committed in the last 25 yrs or so, he&#39;d gotten the urge to kill out of his system, or maybe the last kill, he came damn close to getting caught. If he kept momentos around to look at all the time, he would want to add to them, I would think. I also believe WPD has interviewed him in the past, and he was persuasive enough to get by without detection. So he sat in his easy chair and laughed all week at how stupid WPD was, and how smart he was for not getting caught. <BR>I know there are a few cops who post here, and I&#39;m sure WPD/FBI monitors this site, as they should. <BR>Ask yourself this question. &#34;If I killed someone, would I keep stuff that would incriminate me in my own home?&#34; <BR>I guess some people are stupid enough, but I don&#39;t think BTK is.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5815-->
<!--Post: 5830--><!--Time: 1107396000-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5830"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 6:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mel Ignatow, Gerard Schaefer and Mike DeBardeleben weren&#39;t stupid but I agree with you mean about such behavior! The first two kept completely incriminating souvenirs in their houses and the latter in a rented storage shed. I think it&#39;s a risk they&#39;re willing to take. The stuff is usually so well hidden it would require taking up the floors and ripping open the walls for LE to find it and that means search warrants and if they have enough cause for such warrants, BTK is as good as caught anyway. <BR> <BR>There&#39;s a chance BTK has stuff in a safe deposit box <i>and</i> in his home. You never know. These sexual sadists, historically, are completely untrusting of anyone, no matter what. I see BTK as also utterly untrusting of anyone but you still could be right. Every human being is unique and isn&#39;t neatly categorized. <BR> <BR>I agree BTK has had contact with the police in some way. Definitely. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5830-->
<!--Post: 5831--><!--Time: 1107396109-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5831"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Doom<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Doom<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 6:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good point Brown_tornado.  Your theory leads to further thinking.  And please think about this because your idea gave me this idea.  Your theory can lead to the reasoning that perhaps, even though BTK does in fact commit the crimes of a sexual sadistic serial killer &#40;other serial killers mainly&#41;, he does not posses the same make up of a true sexual sadist...He is in fact mimicking what he thinks a true sexual sadist would do.  He in fact does not need his trophies near him because they do not give him the same psychological thrill it would give a real sexual sadist.  He is after all giving all his trophies back to LE.  Meaning what?  They are not of value to him…The attititude and knowledge he is more intelligent than LE is…The taunting is the value he seeks because his life has been ineffectual in his own eyes. Our boy has poor self esteem.   <BR> <BR>Doom<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5831-->
<!--Post: 5876--><!--Time: 1107439659-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5876"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 6:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I doubt that BTK keeps his treasures in a safety deposit box. I think that he keeps them close at hand, at his home. There are so many hiding places in a house that I believe LE could search and not find what they are looking for. BTK could have built a hidden vault that is easily overlooked. Remember H. H. Holmes? <BR> <BR>How many houses has LE searched? Only one that I am aware of.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5876-->
<!--Post: 5883--><!--Time: 1107442942-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5883"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brady<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brady<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 7:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree with Essevi.  With everything I&#39;ve read so far on BTK, I just don&#39;t see him being that sophisticated as to keeping his &#34;mementos&#34; in a SDB.  I think maybe he has/had a shed on his property, possibly locked in a tool box or some other sort of box.  Most men have a place where only they hang out in their home &#40;I like to call them &#34;man caves&#34;&#41;.  It could be his garage, shed or basement.  If he is brazen enough to break into homes and murder innocent people, he is brazen enough to keep his &#34;treasures&#34; close to him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5883-->
<!--Post: 5886--><!--Time: 1107444044-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5886"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 7:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Definitely...I agree that BTK is BRAZEN enough to keep his treasures close to him.  Remember....he is an arrogant s.o.b. - he thinks he has outsmarted everyone...he is thoroughly enjoying LE&#39;s hunt for him...the public&#39;s fascination with him and the posts on this site....perhaps we are all giving Mr. Arrogant way to much attention...for &#40;besides the thrill of torture and killing&#41; attention pleases him most.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5886-->
<!--Post: 6053--><!--Time: 1107497977-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6053"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 10:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Brown_Tornado wrote, <BR><i>Ask yourself this question. &#34;If I killed someone, would I keep stuff that would incriminate me in my own home?&#34;</i>  <BR> <BR>Exactly. Then again, one could ask &#34;If I killed someone, would I keep stuff that would incriminate me, PERIOD?&#34; It&#39;s a small percentage of murderers who keep souvenirs. Therefore, since BTK has proven he&#39;ll take the inherent risk of keeping souvenirs in the first place - not all serial killers keep souvenirs, despite what some books say - I don&#39;t see how keeping the souvenirs at home would trouble BTK. He doesn&#39;t expect to be apprehended. He recently taunted Charlie Otero via a New Mexico stamp &#40;not an absolute fact but I agree with Tom that it&#39;s a taunt&#41;. Brazen? With a capital &#34;B!&#34; Let&#39;s catach him so we may have the knowledge of when he dies. Death with a capital &#34;D!&#34; <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6053-->
<!--Post: 6182--><!--Time: 1107566375-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6182"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:jsk@jvlnet.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 5:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->One thing that occurred to me was, what if hes a pack-rat? at least to an extent...I know i have boxes that my wife has no idea what in them &#40;ham radio stuff!&#41; Small mementos of a murder could easily be kept secret from my spouse, if i did that sort of stuff...They only way they would be found is if i died. The other thing to think about is, if he lived several hours from Wichita there would be LESS media coverage of the crimes thus IF his wife did run across the stuff the names on stuff might not get her attention. Just a thougt!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6182-->
<!--Post: 6334--><!--Time: 1107704479-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6334"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bpb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bpb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 7:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->As far as I can tell &#40;and correct me if I am wrong, please&#41; the things that were takenwere small in size, making them pretty easy to hide anywhere.  Why would you entrust anything of this magnitude to anyone else &#40;even as secure as a SDB&#41;?  I would think you&#39;d keep these things close, to reminisce, to enjoy, to do whatever it is he does...Plus, imagine if they aren&#39;t in one big stash?  So his wife/relative/friend finds a watch?  So what, it&#39;s a watch.  An ID card would be another ball of wax, but if you found, say 1 ID, it would be easy enough to explain away &#40;found it and forgot about it before I could return it&#41;, especially if the ID card was not troubling to the finder.  Just my 2 cents on my first post.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6334-->
